@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@
+# Migrating to portnum v2
+
+Update the module dependency and import path from `example.com/portnum` to
+`example.com/portnum/v2`. `Parse` now returns `(int, error)`:
+
+```go
+port, err := portnum.Parse(configuredPort)
+if err != nil {
+	return fmt.Errorf("parse port: %w", err)
+}
+usePort(port)
+```
+
+Previously, invalid input silently produced zero. In v2, callers must handle
+the error; failed parses return zero and a non-nil error. Accepted input is
+one or more ASCII decimal digits representing 0 through 65535. Leading zeros
+remain valid; empty strings, signs, whitespace, non-digits, and out-of-range
+values are rejected. The v1 release remains available at its original import
+path; v2 does not provide a legacy `Parse` shim.
